# oracle: pair_style body/rounded/polyhedron (no friction, no history) for two rounded cubes (edge 2, rounded diameter 0.5) approaching face to face along x from centres 6 apart at speed 2, examples/body/in.cubes settings (c_n 20, c_t 5, mu 0, A_ua 1, cut 0.5, k_n 100, k_na 1), fix nve/body, 1500 steps: thermo pe ke etotal press and the atom state
# Measured (engine vs native, max relative error, tests/oracle header rel=1e-8): thermo below 1e-14 (ke and pe at the last digit: 1e-15 fails on one ke value), per-atom state (x, v, f) below 1e-14. Contact phase from step ~750 (pe to -0.25, cohesive well, damping c_n 20).
# oracle-inputs: w121body_cubes_approach.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 8
atom_modify     map array
read_data       w121body_cubes_approach.data
set             atom 1 vx 2.0 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
set             atom 2 vx -2.0 vy 0.0 vz 0.0
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
comm_modify     vel yes
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
run             2000
